Locum cover that hasn't reached Allocate — the three fixes Ali agreed to on 11 Sept.

1. The "Add a one-off person" name box now searches the staff list. Type a few letters and
   anyone already on the unit is offered, with their grade and skills shown so two similar
   names are told apart. Picking them uses THEIR record, so the allocator sees the grade.
   Adding somebody genuinely new is still the last row.

2. The Optima check no longer flags people who were put in by hand. Anyone added that way is
   by definition not on Allocate for the day — that is why they had to be typed in — so the
   check was restating its own input as a fault and offering "Remove from day", i.e. offering
   to delete the cover that had just been arranged. It still raises a shift Allocate really
   has dropped.

3. Wording on both cards: they say Allocate rather than Optima, the mismatch card says the
   choice sticks, and its buttons name the two sides instead of two codes.

